# Shifter — Caddyfile (Plan 22 placeholder)
#
# This file exists today only so that `compose/bundled.yml`'s Caddy service
# can mount it without failing at container start. Plan 22 (caddyfile) will
# replace the body with the production reverse-proxy + automatic-TLS
# configuration (acme/byo/internal modes per D-21/D-22, XFF for Plan 09's
# trust boundary, /assets/* + /index.html cache headers honored from the
# Shifter binary, etc.).
#
# Until Plan 22 ships, this minimal config:
#
#   • Listens on :80 only (no automatic TLS attempt → no ACME calls / no
#     network egress required for `just compose-smoke-bundled`)
#   • Proxies every request to the shifter service on the compose network
#   • Forwards X-Forwarded-For so Plan 09's `clientIP()` helper sees the
#     real remote address
#
# Operators MUST NOT deploy this placeholder — Plan 22's production
# Caddyfile is a hard prerequisite for INST-* / OPS-* sign-off. The
# bundled smoke test polls Shifter directly on :8080, so Caddy's
# placeholder behavior here is not exercised by automated verification.

{
	# Disable automatic HTTPS — Plan 22 will enable it conditionally
	# based on SHIFTER_TLS_MODE. Smoke test only needs :80 to bind.
	auto_https off
}

:80 {
	reverse_proxy shifter:8080 {
		header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}
